The blocked sequential GDN kernel adapts the eight-lane state recurrence
from oMLX v0.6.1, omlx/custom_kernels/qwen35_prefill/gdn.py:
https://github.com/jundot/omlx

The upstream file is licensed under Apache-2.0. A copy of that license is
included in licenses/omlx-Apache-2.0.txt. The psi implementation adds F32
normalization and gates, model-derived geometry, ragged request metadata,
BF16 state arenas, arbitrary state snapshots, and per-token F32 replay logs.

The register-based small affine QMM adapts SG8 from oMLX 0.7.1.dev1,
omlx/patches/qwen35_verify_qmm.py:
https://github.com/jundot/omlx

The upstream file is licensed under Apache-2.0. Its SG8 operand encoding and
input-sum correction are adapted from incoai/Splash (Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/incoai/splash

The scalar K-partition and SIMDgroup-column designs are adapted upstream from MTPLX,
Copyright 2026 Youssof Altoukhi (Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/youssofal/mtplx

See licenses/omlx-Apache-2.0.txt. The PSI adaptation adds stacked gate/up
bindings, a compile-time SwiGLU epilogue, and submission-time active rows.

The QSA indexer Steel scoring kernels adapt oMLX commit
d6b2b92b11ebcbf4a4c1f002b0d590a3117212a8 (Apache-2.0),
Copyright © 2026 Apple Inc. See licenses/omlx-Apache-2.0.txt.
The psi implementation adds paged keys and request-local score task templates.

The QSA indexer vector scoring and sampled exact radix selection adapt
TensorFold 0.6.6, kernels/qwen/flash_next/v1/attention.py and block_select.py:
https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold
Copyright 2026 TensorFold contributors (Apache-2.0).
See licenses/tensorfold-Apache-2.0.txt. The psi implementation uses paged keys,
existing token metadata, replay capacities, and chronological logical group IDs.

The n-gram embedding follows hash parameter construction and arithmetic in
oMLX commit 64bf5d1ba6336b45955c00f7fe0e46acd5c85095 (Apache-2.0).
See licenses/omlx-Apache-2.0.txt. The psi implementation uses caller-owned
metadata, resident table groups, and capacity-selected Metal replay kernels.
The grouped resident lookup also follows the eight-table design in TensorFold
0.6.6 (Apache-2.0). See licenses/tensorfold-Apache-2.0.txt.

The PLE baseline follows the same oMLX arithmetic. The psi implementation
separates preparation, application, and accepted-prefix state commit through
caller-owned Metal replay.
